 <class>LimitMonitorSettings</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="LimitMonitorSettings">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect>
    <x>0</x>
    <y>0</y>
    <width>400</width>
    <height>230</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <item>
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="chkEscape">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Show $T escape buttons (ALOE FIXED7+ firmware)</string>
     </property>
     <property name="checked">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="lblNote">
     <property name="text">
      <string>The $T buttons send $TX-/$TX+/$TY-/$TY+/$TZ-/$TZ+ commands of the ALOE FIXED7+ firmware: the axis slowly backs off the pressed switch (up to 10 mm + pull-off) entirely inside the firmware. In Alarm state the button first sends a soft reset (Ctrl-X) automatically to leave the hard-limit critical lock. On stock GRBL these commands are rejected with error:2 and cause no motion.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="wordWrap">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="chkDoor">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Monitor the safety door pin (Pn:D)</string>
     </property>
     <property name="checked">
      <bool>false</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="lblNoteDoor">
     <property name="text">
      <string>GRBL reports the door pin only while it considers the door OPEN, and only if the firmware was built with ENABLE_SAFETY_DOOR_INPUT_PIN (disabled in stock GRBL and in ALOE FIXED7+). Leave this off if the machine has no door sensor - otherwise the panel would show a false green "all ok" for a contact nobody is actually reading.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="wordWrap">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <spacer name="spacerBottom">
     <property name="orientation">
      <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
      <size>
       <width>0</width>
       <height>0</height>
      </size>
     </property>
    </spacer>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
